>> title: Hummus
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: chickpeas, tahini, middle eastern, dip, food processor
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: simmer 45 min until falling apart
>> step.2: blend, then stand 10 min
>> step.3: purée until completely smooth
>> step.4: blend in
>> step.5: whip in until pale and fluffy

Simmer @dried chickpeas{1%cup}(200 g; soaked overnight) with @baking soda{1/2%tsp} in plenty of water for ~{45%min}, until the skins slip and a chickpea crushes between your fingers.

Blend @garlic{2%cloves} with @lemon juice{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} in a #food processor{}, then let it stand ~{10%min}.

Purée @&(~2)drained chickpeas{} into @&(~1)garlic{} for a full two minutes, until no grit is left.

Blend @tahini{2/3%cup}(160 g; well stirred) and @ground cumin{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)purée{}.

Whip @ice water{1/4%cup}(60 mL) into @&(~1)hummus{} until pale and fluffy, then pool @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs} on top.
